meta {
  name: normalize platforms
  type: http
  seq: 21
}

post {
  url: {{collection_url}}/internal/normalize-platforms
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{access_token}}
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.scanned: isNumber
  res.body.normalized: isNumber
  res.body.skipped: isNumber
}

docs {
  Nightly lever (first step of the collection-rematch CronJob's chain,
  ahead of normalize-regions and the entry rematch), operator-runnable
  any time: canonicalizes free-text custom-entry platforms against the
  enrichment platform catalog, exact-or-alias matching only - never
  fuzzy, so an unrecognized name is left untouched rather than
  misfiled. Idempotent: a stamped entry leaves the selection set, so a
  second run normalizes 0 once the catalog covers everything in play.
  Expect 200 with scanned/normalized/skipped; skipped rows are names
  the catalog does not know yet, left for a rerun after it learns
  them.

  Guard: admin role or a service token. The bearer behind
  {{access_token}} must be an admin - the folder's dev-token flow logs
  in as alice by default, so run it with body {"user": "admin"} first,
  or override --env-var access_token with a minted admin or service
  token.
}
